DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The ggeettppwwnnaamm() function returns a pointer to a structure containing the
       broken‐out fields of the record in the password database (e.g., the lo‐
       cal password file _/_e_t_c_/_p_a_s_s_w_d, NIS, and LDAP) that matches the username
       _n_a_m_e.

       The ggeettppwwuuiidd() function returns a pointer to a structure containing the
       broken‐out  fields  of the record in the password database that matches
       the user ID _u_i_d.

       The _p_a_s_s_w_d structure is defined in _<_p_w_d_._h_> as follows:

           struct passwd {
               char   *pw_name;       /* username */
               char   *pw_passwd;     /* user password */
               uid_t   pw_uid;        /* user ID */
               gid_t   pw_gid;        /* group ID */
               char   *pw_gecos;      /* user information */
               char   *pw_dir;        /* home directory */
               char   *pw_shell;      /* shell program */
